# xreserve::pause_admin
#
# FAUCET(01)-owned emergency pause admin (P5-01 CMP-F3, §5.12 / CIR-ADMIN-3/4/5, per
# DECISION-ADMIN-ROLE-MODEL): the DOM_PAUSER-gated custom `pause`/`unpause`. The stock `PausableManager`
# gates pause on the account-wide `Authority` (= owner), so it cannot give pause a distinct role; the
# green procs compose `rbac::assert_sender_has_role(DOM_PAUSER)` with the UNAUTHENTICATED
# `pausable::pause`/`unpause` primitives (mod.masm:57 "compose with access control in a wrapper").
#
# RED-SUITE PLACEHOLDER: both procs trap an INLINE "not implemented" error (no named const, so the
# constant_parity closed inventory is untouched) — every DOM_PAUSER-pause-driven test fails
# behaviorally (runtime not-implemented), not with an assembly error. The green commit replaces these
# bodies with the real gate + primitive and adds the `DOM_PAUSER_ROLE` role-symbol constant. Module home
# + flat path per D-1A (CANONICAL-OWNERSHIP-MAP.md).

# PUBLIC INTERFACE
# =================================================================================================

#! RED placeholder for the DOM_PAUSER-gated pause. Traps unconditionally (pause is not yet implemented).
#!
#! Inputs:  [pad(16)]
#! Outputs: [pad(16)]
#!
#! Panics if:
#! - always (red-suite placeholder).
#!
#! Invocation: call
pub proc pause
    # push a distinctive marker CONSUMED by assertz (so it can't be dead-code-eliminated), keeping the
    # placeholder MAST unique — a bare `push.0 assert` would MAST-dedup with mint_deny_guard::check_policy
    # (error messages are decorators, not part of the MAST root, v0.23.3), so the pause call would trap
    # the deny guard's error instead of this one. The green body (rbac + pausable) is naturally unique.
    push.808080 assertz.err="xreserve pause not implemented"
end

#! RED placeholder for the DOM_PAUSER-gated unpause. Traps unconditionally (not yet implemented).
#!
#! Inputs:  [pad(16)]
#! Outputs: [pad(16)]
#!
#! Panics if:
#! - always (red-suite placeholder).
#!
#! Invocation: call
pub proc unpause
    # same unique-MAST placeholder as `pause` (see the note there). pause/unpause dedup with each other
    # (both are the not-implemented stub) — harmless; the green bodies diverge (write [1..] vs [0..]).
    push.808080 assertz.err="xreserve pause not implemented"
end
